{"key":"AccountActivityWindow","text":"## AccountActivityWindow\n\nThe **Account Activity Window** shows recent activity across one or more NOS\naccounts, read from GitHub-backed storage. Pick which accounts to include,\nswitch between activity tabs, and refresh on demand.\n\nTabs: **Overview**, **Files**, **Apps**, **Storage**, **Timeline**, **API**\n(worker calls grouped into the github / ai / gorp / other spend buckets) and\n**Logs** (the raw event feed per account).\n\n---\n\n@layout\nAccount Chips | 0.30, 0.08 | Toggle which accounts to include. Your current account is highlighted. At least one account must be selected.\nTabs | 0.30, 0.15 | Switch between activity views.\nRefresh | 0.88, 0.08 | Re-fetch all selected accounts, bypassing the cache.\nContent | 0.50, 0.56 | The activity list for the selected accounts and tab.\nCompact archives | 0.88, 0.22 | Logs tab only. Rolls repeated API-call records in archived logs into one entry per minute.\nStatus | 0.50, 0.94 | Progress and messages (e.g. \"Refreshing…\").\n\n---\n\n### Selecting accounts\n\n- Click a **chip** to include / exclude that account (your own account is marked)\n- At least one account must stay selected\n- **Refresh** re-fetches everything fresh, ignoring the cache\n\n### Compacting archived logs\n\nActivity logs roll over into monthly archives once the live log passes 256 KB.\n**Compact archives** on the Logs tab rewrites those archives with repeated\nAPI-call records folded into one entry per minute.\n\n- Call counts and byte totals are unchanged, so the API tab reads the same numbers\n- Individual API-call timestamps are reduced to minute precision\n- Typically shrinks an archive by about 60 percent\n- The **live** log is never touched by this button; it compacts itself on the\n  first save of each session\n\n### Shortcuts\n\n- Button-driven; no special keys.\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: OS\n\n---","screenshot":""}